I reverted V_CORNER_MIN to 55.0, recorded V3.6 as REVERT in CHANGELOG.md, and applied V3.7 (STEER_SMOOTH 0.5 → 0.3). The
self-test passes all 7 checks. I did not run the race, and the changelog says "not run yet" for V3.7.                   
                                                                                                                        
V3.6 REVERT. The lap was 1:45.684, 3.092 s slower than V3.5, with 0 damage. Peak |trackPos| at Turn 11 fell from 0.891  
to 0.761, but the apex speed barely changed (61.8 km/h against 61.1). The lost time came before the corner. Per 200 m,  
V3.6 was slower than V3.5 by +0.22 s at 2600–2800 m, +0.46 s at 2800–3000 m and +0.73 s at 3000–3200 m. It was also     
0.02–0.15 s slower on every earlier segment. The first logged speed in the 3140–3200 m bin was 128.7 km/h in V3.6       
against 179.7 km/h in V3.5. The log has no side rays, so it can't show why the approach was slower. The lower corner    
floor is the only change, so it is the likely cause.                                                                    
                                                                                                                        
V3.7: STEER_SMOOTH 0.5 → 0.3. I rejected TRACK_MARGIN and EXTRA_CENTERING_GAIN because the telemetry shows they cannot  
act at Turn 11:                                                                                                         
- Edge term is inactive during the ramp. The extra centering only applies once |trackPos| exceeds 0.70. During the      
  steering ramp (3249–3264 m), |trackPos| stays at or below 0.57.                                                       
- Steer is already saturated. Steer reaches 1.0 at 3265.3 m in V3.5 and 3263.9 m in V3.6, and the raw value is also     
  clipped at 1.0. |trackPos| only passes 0.70 around 3280 m in V3.5. Changing the margin or gain cannot alter a command 
  that is already clipped.                                                                                              
- Filter lag is the available lever. Raw steer ramps up at about 0.05 per tick, and the logged steer trails it by       
  0.02–0.08. For example, at 3251.9 m in V3.5 the raw value was 0.39 and the steer 0.31. The lag drops from about 1.0   
  tick at 0.5 to about 0.43 tick at 0.3.                                                                                
- V3.6 reached steer 1.0 earlier. It got there about 1.4 m sooner, at trackPos +0.167 against +0.111 in V3.5. Its entry 
  speed was also lower, so the two effects can't be separated from this data.                                           
                                                                                                                        
Expected effect (hypothesis, not measured).                                                                             
- Peak |trackPos|: The lag shrinks by about 0.57 tick, roughly 0.6 m at 80 km/h. That may lower the 0.891 peak slightly.
  I would not expect it to reach V3.6's 0.761.                                                                          
- Lap time: Corner speed and braking are the same as V3.5, so I expect it near 1:42.592 and claim no gain.              
- Risk: Less filtering on straights could add some weaving. The changelog says to revert if damage is above 0, or if the
  lap is slower than 1:42.592 and the Turn 11 peak is not below 0.85.                                                   
                                                                                                                        
